Judge a world-readable key repository by its key files

FernetUtils.validate_key_repository in keystone/common/fernet_utils.py
logs "key_repository is world readable: <path>" at WARNING whenever the
key directory has S_IROTH or S_IXOTH, and never looks at a file in it.
load_keys calls it on every call: the token formatter on every token
issue and every uncached validation, the receipt formatter, the
credential provider on every encryption and decryption, and the key
commands of keystone-manage. The kubelet creates the mount point of a
Secret volume with mode 1777, ORs the setgid and group bits in under
fsGroup and applies defaultMode to the files only. Measured on
2026-11-17 in a kind cluster (Kubernetes v1.37.0): the API pod the
keystone-operator renders has a key directory of 3777 root:42424, a
Secret mounted one level down through items[].path gives 2755, and an
emptyDir mount point gives 2777. No field of a pod spec reaches a mode
the check accepts, so the warning fires on every key load of every
CobaltCore OpenStack Keystone pod: three replicas wrote about 967,000
of these lines in 24 hours (C5C3/cobaltcore#1786).

The warning is false there. The keystone-operator projects every key
as 0440 root:42424: `defaultMode: 0400` on the fernet-keys and
credential-keys volumes
(operators/keystone/internal/controller/reconcile_deployment.go) and
`fsGroup: 42424` on the pod (internal/common/deployment/workload.go).
Before those settings the keys were 0644 root:root, readable by every
user of the container.

validate_key_repository now warns only when the directory is open to
others and _has_world_readable_key finds a regular file in it that
others can read. The message text, the return value and the LOG.error
for a repository the process cannot access are unchanged. Every regular
file counts, not only the digit-named keys, because the 0.tmp of a
running rotation is key material too. os.stat follows symlinks, so the
mode of a Secret volume's key (0 -> ..data/0) is the mode of the
projected file; the ..data link and the timestamped directory are not
regular files and are skipped. An entry os.stat cannot resolve is
skipped and logged at DEBUG: a FileNotFoundError, because a rotation or
the kubelet's ..data swap can remove a file between os.listdir and
os.stat, and any other OSError, such as a link loop or a link into a
directory Keystone cannot search, because load_keys skips that entry
as well (os.path.isfile is False for it). An OSError of os.listdir
reaches the caller, like the os.stat of the directory above it. A
private repository (0700) never reaches the file check.

An init container that copies the keys into a 0750 memory emptyDir
would end in-place key rotation, because every rotation would need a
rollout. A sidecar that mirrors the Secret into such a directory adds a
container to every API pod and a sync that can serve stale keys.

Tests: no upstream test moves. ksfixtures.KeyRepository builds its
repository with fixtures.TempDir(), whose mode is 0700, and
keystone/tests/unit/test_cli.py mocks validate_key_repository, so no
test reaches the warning. The patch adds nine tests to
FernetUtilsTestCase in keystone/tests/unit/common/test_utils.py, each
on a TempDir whose modes it sets with os.chmod:

- test_world_readable_repository_with_private_keys_logs_no_warning:
  a 0755 directory with a 0400 key loads the key without the warning.
- test_secret_volume_layout_with_private_keys_logs_no_warning: a 0755
  directory in the kubelet's Secret volume layout (0 -> ..data/0,
  ..data -> a 0755 directory) with a 0400 key loads the key without
  the warning.
- test_world_readable_repository_with_world_readable_key_logs_warning:
  a 0755 directory with a 0644 key logs the warning with its path.
- test_world_readable_temporary_key_logs_warning: a 0644 0.tmp beside
  a 0400 key in a 0755 directory logs the warning.
- test_private_repository_with_world_readable_key_logs_no_warning:
  a 0700 directory with a 0644 key stays silent, as upstream.
- test_world_readable_empty_repository_logs_no_warning: an empty 0755
  directory is valid and stays silent.
- test_missing_repository_is_reported_without_a_mode_check: a missing
  directory returns False with the unchanged error and raises nothing.
- test_key_removed_after_listing_is_skipped: a symlink whose target is
  gone beside a 0400 key raises nothing and stays silent.
- test_unresolvable_key_entry_is_skipped: a symlink loop beside a 0400
  key raises nothing and stays silent.

With only the test hunks applied, the first, the second, the sixth, the
eighth and the ninth fail.

Proof: test_key_repository_mode_patch_applied in
tests/container-images/verify_keystone.sh calls validate_key_repository
in the built image on a 0755 directory in the Secret volume layout,
asserts no warning for a 0400 key and the warning once the key is 0444.

The fernet_utils.py and test_utils.py blobs are the same in keystone
29.0.0 and 30.0.0, and the twins under patches/keystone/2026.1/ and
patches/keystone/2026.2/ differ only in their Applies-to line.

Applies to keystone 29.0.0 (2026.1).

Upstream status: not yet proposed.

diff --git a/keystone/common/fernet_utils.py b/keystone/common/fernet_utils.py
index 36dd70671..0b1da2af3 100644
--- a/keystone/common/fernet_utils.py
+++ b/keystone/common/fernet_utils.py
@@ -62,18 +62,39 @@ class FernetUtils:
                 },
             )
         else:
-            # ensure the key repository isn't world-readable
+            # Warn only when others may list or enter the repository and
+            # a regular file in it is readable by others; a repository
+            # without such a file exposes no key material.
             stat_info = os.stat(self.key_repository)
             if (
                 stat_info.st_mode & stat.S_IROTH
                 or stat_info.st_mode & stat.S_IXOTH
-            ):
+            ) and self._has_world_readable_key():
                 LOG.warning(
                     'key_repository is world readable: %s', self.key_repository
                 )
 
         return is_valid
 
+    def _has_world_readable_key(self):
+        """Tell whether others can read a file of the key repository."""
+        for filename in os.listdir(self.key_repository):
+            path = os.path.join(self.key_repository, filename)
+            try:
+                file_info = os.stat(path)
+            except OSError as e:
+                # A rotation or the kubelet removed the file after listdir,
+                # or the entry cannot be resolved (a link loop, a link into
+                # a directory Keystone cannot search). load_keys skips such
+                # an entry as well, because os.path.isfile is False for it.
+                LOG.debug('Skipping %s in the key mode check: %s', path, e)
+                continue
+            if stat.S_ISREG(file_info.st_mode) and (
+                file_info.st_mode & stat.S_IROTH
+            ):
+                return True
+        return False
+
     def create_key_directory(
         self, keystone_user_id=None, keystone_group_id=None
     ):
